1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:07,974
What's today's video about? A day in the life of someone working abroad.

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: The Start of a New Day

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:14,560
I open my eyes.

4
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:18,183
All I see is a white ceiling.

5
00:00:18,206 --> 00:00:22,073
This is Tokyo.

6
00:00:22,096 --> 00:00:26,296
My name is Rin.

7
00:00:26,319 --> 00:00:29,158
I came here from America.

8
00:00:29,181 --> 00:00:32,352
The room is so quiet.

9
00:00:32,376 --> 00:00:36,542
All I can hear is the ticking of the clock.

10
00:00:36,565 --> 00:00:39,344
I open the window.

11
00:00:39,367 --> 00:00:43,614
A cold breeze blows in.

12
00:00:43,638 --> 00:00:47,644
A new day begins.

13
00:00:47,667 --> 00:00:52,513
Today, I’ll keep living in this big city.

14
00:00:52,537 --> 00:00:55,612
I sip my coffee.

15
00:00:55,636 --> 00:00:58,646
It’s warm.

16
00:00:58,669 --> 00:01:03,002
I get ready and head outside.

17
00:01:03,026 --> 00:01:05,966
I walk to the station.

18
00:01:05,989 --> 00:01:09,389
There are so many people.

19
00:01:09,412 --> 00:01:13,246
Where is everyone going?

20
00:01:13,269 --> 00:01:16,635
No one knows me.

21
00:01:16,658 --> 00:01:19,708
It feels a little lonely.

22
00:01:19,732 --> 00:01:24,189
Oh, good morning, Rin!

23
00:01:24,212 --> 00:01:28,900
Oh, good morning, Mr. Tanaka!

24
00:01:28,924 --> 00:01:31,376
You’re early again today.

25
00:01:31,399 --> 00:01:35,850
Yeah, I love the morning air.

26
00:01:35,873 --> 00:01:38,942
I see. That’s nice.

27
00:01:38,966 --> 00:01:43,011
You’re always early too, Mr. Tanaka.

28
00:01:43,034 --> 00:01:48,367
Yeah, I prefer the morning trains.

29
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:50,957
There are fewer people.

30
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:56,580
True. Crowded trains can be a little scary.

31
00:01:56,603 --> 00:02:01,203
Even Japanese people don’t like packed trains.

32
00:02:01,226 --> 00:02:04,629
Really? That makes me feel better.

33
00:02:04,653 --> 00:02:07,219
Here comes the train.

34
00:02:07,242 --> 00:02:10,279
Yeah, let’s go together.

35
00:02:10,303 --> 00:02:13,570
I heard Mr. Tanaka’s voice.

36
00:02:13,593 --> 00:02:17,926
The loneliness faded a little.

37
00:02:17,949 --> 00:02:21,082
I’m not alone.

38
00:02:21,106 --> 00:02:24,473
Off to work I go.

39
00:02:24,496 --> 00:02:25,996
Scene 2: The Kanji Barrier and Work

40
00:02:25,996 --> 00:02:28,533
I’ve arrived at the office.

41
00:02:28,556 --> 00:02:30,923
I open my laptop.

42
00:02:30,946 --> 00:02:33,919
There are so many emails.

43
00:02:33,942 --> 00:02:36,987
All in Japanese.

44
00:02:37,011 --> 00:02:40,683
Kanji is really tough.

45
00:02:40,706 --> 00:02:44,673
I work in design.

46
00:02:44,695 --> 00:02:47,362
Design is what I’m good at.

47
00:02:47,386 --> 00:02:51,157
But the language barrier is high.

48
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:54,747
Sometimes, I feel like crying.

49
00:02:54,770 --> 00:02:57,903
I let out a big sigh.

50
00:02:57,926 --> 00:03:01,093
Rin, are you okay?

51
00:03:01,116 --> 00:03:06,249
Oh, Tanaka-san. Yes, it's alright.

52
00:03:06,272 --> 00:03:10,080
You were sighing deeply.

53
00:03:10,104 --> 00:03:15,171
I'm sorry. Some kanji are a bit difficult for me.

54
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:17,427
Which kanji?

55
00:03:17,450 --> 00:03:20,458
The kanji in this email.

56
00:03:20,482 --> 00:03:25,765
Ah, this one reads 'kakunin'.

57
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:28,222
'Kakunin'?

58
00:03:28,245 --> 00:03:32,578
Yes. It means 'to check' or 'confirm'.

59
00:03:32,601 --> 00:03:34,671
I see. Thank you.

60
00:03:34,694 --> 00:03:37,227
You can use a dictionary, you know.

61
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:40,549
Yes, I always do.

62
00:03:40,573 --> 00:03:44,340
If you don’t understand something, feel free to ask anytime.

63
00:03:44,363 --> 00:03:48,051
Tanaka-san, you're always so kind.

64
00:03:48,074 --> 00:03:52,052
We're on the same team. It's only natural.

65
00:03:52,076 --> 00:03:54,681
I really appreciate it.

66
00:03:54,705 --> 00:03:57,992
We have a meeting this afternoon, right?

67
00:03:58,015 --> 00:04:01,182
Yes, I’ve finished the materials.

68
00:04:01,205 --> 00:04:04,538
Great, let me take a look later.

69
00:04:04,561 --> 00:04:06,832
Understood.

70
00:04:06,856 --> 00:04:11,728
I’m not working alone.

71
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:14,390
There are people who help me.

72
00:04:14,414 --> 00:04:18,580
That’s why I want to study more.

73
00:04:18,603 --> 00:04:22,883
I want to speak Japanese more fluently.

74
00:04:22,907 --> 00:04:25,240
I’ll do my best today too.

75
00:04:25,263 --> 00:04:26,763
Scene 3: Lunch in the Park

76
00:04:26,763 --> 00:04:29,530
It’s lunchtime.

77
00:04:29,553 --> 00:04:32,120
I’m at the park.

78
00:04:32,143 --> 00:04:35,281
The weather is lovely today.

79
00:04:35,304 --> 00:04:37,970
The sky is so blue.

80
00:04:37,993 --> 00:04:41,127
It reminds me of the skies back in America.

81
00:04:41,151 --> 00:04:44,518
I made a bento.

82
00:04:44,541 --> 00:04:48,314
Tamagoyaki and onigiri.

83
00:04:48,337 --> 00:04:52,571
Japanese food is so beautifully presented.

84
00:04:52,594 --> 00:04:55,462
It almost feels too pretty to eat.

85
00:04:55,485 --> 00:04:59,285
Rin-san, is this spot okay?

86
00:04:59,308 --> 00:05:03,395
Tanaka-san! Yes, please, have a seat.

87
00:05:03,419 --> 00:05:08,076
Food always tastes better when eaten outside, doesn’t it?

88
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:11,975
Yes, the breeze feels wonderful.

89
00:05:11,998 --> 00:05:15,972
Rin-san, your bento looks amazing!

90
00:05:15,995 --> 00:05:18,729
I made it myself.

91
00:05:18,751 --> 00:05:22,362
Your tamagoyaki looks perfect.

92
00:05:22,386 --> 00:05:24,153
Thank you.

93
00:05:24,176 --> 00:05:28,257
Though I’m a little worried about the taste.

94
00:05:28,281 --> 00:05:31,455
May I try a piece?

95
00:05:31,478 --> 00:05:34,377
Of course, go ahead.

96
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,268
Give it a try.

97
00:05:36,291 --> 00:05:38,424
Let’s dig in!

98
00:05:38,447 --> 00:05:42,614
Mmm, it’s really delicious!

99
00:05:42,637 --> 00:05:44,415
Really?

100
00:05:44,438 --> 00:05:46,522
That’s a relief!

101
00:05:46,546 --> 00:05:50,679
It's just the right amount of sweetness—perfect.

102
00:05:50,702 --> 00:05:54,635
Someday, I’ll cook American dishes too.

103
00:05:54,658 --> 00:05:57,192
I can’t wait!

104
00:05:57,215 --> 00:06:01,661
Someone out there will taste what I’ve made.

105
00:06:01,684 --> 00:06:04,851
And they’ll tell me it’s delicious.

106
00:06:04,874 --> 00:06:09,240
Those words fill my heart.

107
00:06:09,263 --> 00:06:15,147
In this little lunchbox, I’ve found my place.

108
00:06:15,170 --> 00:06:18,747
With this, I can power through the rest of the workday.

109
00:06:18,771 --> 00:06:20,271
Scene 4: Overcoming Mistakes and Shifting Your Mood

110
00:06:20,271 --> 00:06:24,161
It’s 3 PM.

111
00:06:24,184 --> 00:06:27,671
Rain is falling outside.

112
00:06:27,694 --> 00:06:31,698
I’m in the office kitchen.

113
00:06:31,722 --> 00:06:35,928
I made a mistake at work earlier.

114
00:06:35,952 --> 00:06:40,235
I misunderstood the Japanese meaning.

115
00:06:40,259 --> 00:06:44,196
Ended up creating the wrong design.

116
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:47,594
I’m so frustrated.

117
00:06:47,617 --> 00:06:52,950
I look at myself in the mirror.

118
00:06:52,973 --> 00:06:56,507
My face looks so sad.

119
00:06:56,529 --> 00:07:00,896
Rin, would you like some coffee?

120
00:07:00,919 --> 00:07:03,565
Tanaka-san.

121
00:07:03,588 --> 00:07:07,922
Everyone makes mistakes.

122
00:07:07,945 --> 00:07:11,945
But I feel like I wasted so much time.

123
00:07:11,968 --> 00:07:14,141
It’s okay.

124
00:07:14,165 --> 00:07:18,379
Your designs are amazing, Rin.

125
00:07:18,403 --> 00:07:20,136
Thank you.

126
00:07:20,159 --> 00:07:24,326
I’ve made plenty of mistakes myself.

127
00:07:24,349 --> 00:07:26,915
You have?

128
00:07:26,938 --> 00:07:30,792
Yes. So don’t dwell on it.

129
00:07:30,815 --> 00:07:36,015
Tanaka-san, why are you always so kind?

130
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:40,684
I’ve worked abroad before.

131
00:07:40,708 --> 00:07:43,241
Really?

132
00:07:43,264 --> 00:07:49,431
Yes. I know how hard it is when you can’t communicate.

133
00:07:49,454 --> 00:07:53,220
You *get* how I feel.

134
00:07:53,243 --> 00:07:57,046
So don’t cry alone, okay?

135
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:59,236
Okay. Thank you.

136
00:07:59,259 --> 00:08:03,593
Now, let’s create a new design.

137
00:08:03,616 --> 00:08:06,782
Yes, I’ll get right on it.

138
00:08:06,805 --> 00:08:12,045
The rain outside is still falling.

139
00:08:12,069 --> 00:08:17,568
But the rain in my heart has stopped.

140
00:08:17,591 --> 00:08:21,391
Someone is watching over me.

141
00:08:21,414 --> 00:08:25,892
And that alone makes me stronger.

142
00:08:25,916 --> 00:08:27,416
Scene 5: Confidence in Presentation and Japanese Language

143
00:08:27,416 --> 00:08:31,149
Today is a big day.

144
00:08:31,172 --> 00:08:35,140
I have a presentation for my new design.

145
00:08:35,164 --> 00:08:39,059
My hands are shaking a little.

146
00:08:39,083 --> 00:08:43,016
Back in the U.S., I was so confident.

147
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:48,880
But here, I have to present in Japanese.

148
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:52,637
The language makes me feel small.

149
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:56,557
I take a deep breath.

150
00:08:56,580 --> 00:09:00,980
My strength isn’t just in my words.

151
00:09:01,003 --> 00:09:06,089
My strength is in this design.

152
00:09:06,113 --> 00:09:09,127
Lin, the meeting is about to start.

153
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:13,193
Yes. I'm really nervous.

154
00:09:13,217 --> 00:09:15,550
Just relax.

155
00:09:15,573 --> 00:09:19,206
I might make mistakes in Japanese.

156
00:09:19,229 --> 00:09:23,062
Japanese isn't the most important thing here.

157
00:09:23,085 --> 00:09:24,728
Huh?

158
00:09:24,752 --> 00:09:28,519
What matters is your passion, Lin.

159
00:09:28,542 --> 00:09:31,944
My passion?

160
00:09:31,967 --> 00:09:36,234
Share the feelings you poured into this design.

161
00:09:36,257 --> 00:09:39,691
Okay. I understand.

162
00:09:39,714 --> 00:09:43,714
I'll be right beside you, so don't worry.

163
00:09:43,737 --> 00:09:47,337
I feel at ease when you're here, Tanaka-san.

164
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,193
Shall we go, then?

165
00:09:50,216 --> 00:09:53,391
Yes, thank you.

166
00:09:53,414 --> 00:09:56,748
Opening the door to the meeting room.

167
00:09:56,771 --> 00:09:59,737
Everyone is looking at me.

168
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:03,257
But I'm not scared anymore.

169
00:10:03,281 --> 00:10:08,614
I'll show them the burning passion inside me.

170
00:10:08,637 --> 00:10:13,676
I believe in my design.

171
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:17,933
Everyone, please take a look at my design.

172
00:10:17,956 --> 00:10:20,013
Thank you for your time.

173
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:22,636
The meeting begins.

174
00:10:22,659 --> 00:10:26,793
I stand tall, facing forward.

175
00:10:26,816 --> 00:10:28,316
Scene 6: Sunset and Emotions

176
00:10:28,316 --> 00:10:32,049
The presentation is over.

177
00:10:32,072 --> 00:10:36,672
I'm on the company rooftop.

178
00:10:36,695 --> 00:10:41,095
The sunset is painting the sky red.

179
00:10:41,118 --> 00:10:44,685
Such a beautiful shade of red.

180
00:10:44,708 --> 00:10:50,674
This empty rooftop is my secret place.

181
00:10:50,697 --> 00:10:55,231
The wind gently brushes against my face.

182
00:10:55,254 --> 00:11:01,303
Everyone praised my design.

183
00:11:01,326 --> 00:11:06,222
My Japanese might have been poor, but my passion came through.

184
00:11:06,246 --> 00:11:10,658
I was so happy, I almost cried.

185
00:11:10,682 --> 00:11:14,348
Lin, I've been looking for you.

186
00:11:14,371 --> 00:11:17,305
Oh, Tanaka-san.

187
00:11:17,328 --> 00:11:19,661
So you were here.

188
00:11:19,684 --> 00:11:23,484
Yes, just watching the sunset.

189
00:11:23,507 --> 00:11:28,040
Your presentation today was amazing.

190
00:11:28,063 --> 00:11:30,997
It was all thanks to you.

191
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:35,053
No, it was all your doing.

192
00:11:35,076 --> 00:11:38,131
Thank you so much, really.

193
00:11:38,154 --> 00:11:42,843
Everyone said they loved your design.

194
00:11:42,866 --> 00:11:46,400
Hearing that puts me at ease.

195
00:11:46,423 --> 00:11:50,556
Things are going to get even busier from here.

196
00:11:50,579 --> 00:11:54,579
Yes, I'll do my best.

197
00:11:54,602 --> 00:11:58,969
When you're tired, let's come back here.

198
00:11:58,992 --> 00:12:00,725
That sounds good.

199
00:12:00,748 --> 00:12:03,915
I love this view.

200
00:12:03,938 --> 00:12:07,874
Shall we head back downstairs?

201
00:12:07,897 --> 00:12:09,664
Yes.

202
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:14,853
The sun sets, and the city lights begin to glow.

203
00:12:14,876 --> 00:12:18,282
Tokyo’s night is just beginning.

204
00:12:18,306 --> 00:12:24,717
Though the stars are hidden, the city lights twinkle like them.

205
00:12:24,741 --> 00:12:30,975
In this glow, I feel like I can keep going a little longer.

206
00:12:30,998 --> 00:12:34,816
May tomorrow be another good day.

207
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:36,340
Scene 7: Evening Convenience Store Stroll

208
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:39,306
It’s 8 PM.

209
00:12:39,329 --> 00:12:42,581
I leave the office and start walking.

210
00:12:42,605 --> 00:12:47,338
The cool night air feels refreshing.

211
00:12:47,361 --> 00:12:50,031
I step into a convenience store.

212
00:12:50,054 --> 00:12:54,254
Bright lights and music welcome me.

213
00:12:54,277 --> 00:12:59,010
Japanese convenience stores are magical places.

214
00:12:59,033 --> 00:13:01,367
They have everything you could need.

215
00:13:01,390 --> 00:13:05,625
I pick up a warm tea and some snacks.

216
00:13:05,648 --> 00:13:08,248
Welcome!

217
00:13:08,271 --> 00:13:10,709
This, please.

218
00:13:10,732 --> 00:13:13,366
A tea and some snacks, right?

219
00:13:13,389 --> 00:13:16,322
That’ll be 350 yen.

220
00:13:16,345 --> 00:13:19,878
Here you go.

221
00:13:19,901 --> 00:13:22,040
Here’s your change.

222
00:13:22,064 --> 00:13:24,697
Thank you, as always.

223
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,390
Huh?

224
00:13:26,413 --> 00:13:29,892
Do you remember me?

225
00:13:29,916 --> 00:13:31,683
Yes.

226
00:13:31,706 --> 00:13:35,344
You come by often after work, don’t you?

227
00:13:35,367 --> 00:13:37,734
Yes, that’s right.

228
00:13:37,757 --> 00:13:41,924
You work so late every day—thank you for your hard work.

229
00:13:41,947 --> 00:13:44,280
Thank you.

230
00:13:44,303 --> 00:13:48,103
Take a moment to relax with this warm tea.

231
00:13:48,126 --> 00:13:51,526
That means a lot to me.

232
00:13:51,549 --> 00:13:53,560
Come back anytime.

233
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:56,916
I will. Goodnight.

234
00:13:56,939 --> 00:13:59,632
I step out of the convenience store.

235
00:13:59,656 --> 00:14:04,289
The clerk remembered my face.

236
00:14:04,312 --> 00:14:09,179
I used to think Tokyo was a big, cold city.

237
00:14:09,203 --> 00:14:14,179
But small moments of warmth are everywhere.

238
00:14:14,203 --> 00:14:18,869
The tea in my hands feels so warm.

239
00:14:18,892 --> 00:14:23,726
This city has started to feel a little like home.

240
00:14:23,749 --> 00:14:26,415
The night breeze blows.

241
00:14:26,438 --> 00:14:29,476
I head home.

242
00:14:29,499 --> 00:14:30,999
Scene 8: Sketching on a Day Off

243
00:14:30,999 --> 00:14:34,233
It’s Saturday.

244
00:14:34,255 --> 00:14:38,464
I’m at a nearby café.

245
00:14:38,488 --> 00:14:43,222
Tea on a day off tastes extra special.

246
00:14:43,245 --> 00:14:46,978
I take a seat by the window.

247
00:14:47,001 --> 00:14:50,300
I open my sketchbook.

248
00:14:50,323 --> 00:14:54,731
I love drawing.

249
00:14:54,755 --> 00:14:58,922
I sketch the people walking by with my pen.

250
00:14:58,945 --> 00:15:02,878
Where is everyone going?

251
00:15:02,901 --> 00:15:05,868
Who are they meeting?

252
00:15:05,891 --> 00:15:11,291
In my drawings, time stands still.

253
00:15:11,314 --> 00:15:13,247
Lin-san?

254
00:15:13,270 --> 00:15:16,404
Huh? Oh, Tanaka-san!

255
00:15:16,427 --> 00:15:19,002
What a coincidence!

256
00:15:19,025 --> 00:15:21,892
Do you come here often?

257
00:15:21,915 --> 00:15:26,163
Yes, I often come here on my days off.

258
00:15:26,186 --> 00:15:28,459
Me too.

259
00:15:28,483 --> 00:15:30,931
I just love the coffee here.

260
00:15:30,955 --> 00:15:33,955
Are you here alone too, Tanaka-san?

261
00:15:33,978 --> 00:15:35,578
Yeah.

262
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,001
Mind if I sit here?

263
00:15:38,024 --> 00:15:40,690
Go ahead.

264
00:15:40,713 --> 00:15:43,890
What are you working on?

265
00:15:43,914 --> 00:15:46,347
I'm drawing.

266
00:15:46,370 --> 00:15:48,370
Can I take a look?

267
00:15:48,393 --> 00:15:51,993
Sure, though I’m a little embarrassed.

268
00:15:52,016 --> 00:15:55,483
Wow, that’s amazing!

269
00:15:55,506 --> 00:15:57,949
You’re really talented.

270
00:15:57,972 --> 00:15:59,670
Thank you.

271
00:15:59,693 --> 00:16:01,660
It’s just a hobby.

272
00:16:01,683 --> 00:16:04,450
It’s a drawing of this town, isn’t it?

273
00:16:04,473 --> 00:16:06,806
It feels so warm.

274
00:16:06,829 --> 00:16:11,029
I love this town.

275
00:16:11,052 --> 00:16:14,932
I’m glad to hear that.

276
00:16:14,955 --> 00:16:17,955
What a wonderful coincidence this turned out to be.

277
00:16:17,978 --> 00:16:23,912
This is the first time I’ve run into a coworker on my day off in Japan.

278
00:16:23,935 --> 00:16:29,225
My sketchbook just gained a new memory.

279
00:16:29,248 --> 00:16:33,848
The coffee tastes sweeter than usual today.

280
00:16:33,871 --> 00:16:35,371
Scene 9: The Moon and a Phone Call

281
00:16:35,371 --> 00:16:38,389
It’s 10 at night.

282
00:16:38,413 --> 00:16:42,980
I’m sitting alone on my bed in my room.

283
00:16:43,003 --> 00:16:47,536
Through the window, I see a full moon.

284
00:16:47,559 --> 00:16:50,241
There’s only one moon.

285
00:16:50,264 --> 00:16:55,231
The same moon shines over America too.

286
00:16:55,254 --> 00:17:00,820
Sometimes, I just really miss hearing my family’s voices.

287
00:17:00,843 --> 00:17:05,534
I pick up my smartphone.

288
00:17:05,558 --> 00:17:09,533
I call my dad in America.

289
00:17:09,556 --> 00:17:12,972
Hello, Rin.

290
00:17:12,996 --> 00:17:15,844
Dad, how are you?

291
00:17:15,867 --> 00:17:20,001
Oh, Rin. I’m doing well.

292
00:17:20,024 --> 00:17:23,657
What time is it in America right now?

293
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:26,755
It’s 8 in the morning.

294
00:17:26,779 --> 00:17:29,182
I’m about to head to work.

295
00:17:29,205 --> 00:17:30,846
I see.

296
00:17:30,870 --> 00:17:34,153
Sorry to call during your busy time.

297
00:17:34,177 --> 00:17:36,985
It’s no problem.

298
00:17:37,008 --> 00:17:39,304
How’s Japan?

299
00:17:39,327 --> 00:17:42,061
It’s a lot of fun.

300
00:17:42,084 --> 00:17:46,822
There are moments I feel lonely, but I’m doing my best.

301
00:17:46,846 --> 00:17:50,248
Don’t push yourself too hard, okay?

302
00:17:50,271 --> 00:17:51,304
Yes.

303
00:17:51,327 --> 00:17:55,967
Work’s starting to feel more manageable, little by little.

304
00:17:55,991 --> 00:17:58,391
That’s great to hear.

305
00:17:58,414 --> 00:18:03,104
Your mom worries about you too, you know.

306
00:18:03,127 --> 00:18:07,332
Tell her I’m doing fine.

307
00:18:07,355 --> 00:18:09,322
Got it.

308
00:18:09,345 --> 00:18:12,594
Goodnight, Rin.

309
00:18:12,618 --> 00:18:13,985
Thank you.

310
00:18:14,008 --> 00:18:16,241
Goodnight.

311
00:18:16,264 --> 00:18:18,831
The call ended.

312
00:18:18,854 --> 00:18:22,987
The room fell silent again.

313
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:28,177
But my heart feels warm.

314
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:32,285
Even when we're far apart, we're still connected.

315
00:18:32,308 --> 00:18:36,244
I'm not alone.

316
00:18:36,267 --> 00:18:41,234
So much love is protecting me.

317
00:18:41,257 --> 00:18:45,108
The moon shines softly.

318
00:18:45,131 --> 00:18:48,531
I'll do my best tomorrow.

319
00:18:48,554 --> 00:18:50,054
Scene 10: A New Morning's First Step

320
00:18:50,054 --> 00:18:52,137
Morning has come.

321
00:18:52,161 --> 00:18:55,166
It's the same morning as always.

322
00:18:55,189 --> 00:18:58,990
But something feels different.

323
00:18:59,013 --> 00:19:05,413
I no longer feel the chill of this city's wind.

324
00:19:05,436 --> 00:19:09,470
I put on my new shoes.

325
00:19:09,493 --> 00:19:13,926
I open the door and step outside.

326
00:19:13,949 --> 00:19:18,416
The sunlight is so bright.

327
00:19:18,439 --> 00:19:24,306
Half a year has passed since I came to Japan.

328
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:27,179
There have been days I cried.

329
00:19:27,203 --> 00:19:30,403
And days I laughed.

330
00:19:30,426 --> 00:19:35,237
Every moment has been precious to me.

331
00:19:35,261 --> 00:19:37,999
I walk toward the station.

332
00:19:38,023 --> 00:19:41,956
Oh, Rin! Good morning.

333
00:19:41,979 --> 00:19:45,193
Good morning, Tanaka-san.

334
00:19:45,217 --> 00:19:48,688
The weather is wonderful today, isn’t it?

335
00:19:48,711 --> 00:19:52,750
Yes, it feels so refreshing.

336
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:55,207
It’s going to be a busy day.

337
00:19:55,230 --> 00:19:58,164
Yes, I’m ready.

338
00:19:58,187 --> 00:20:00,320
That’s reassuring.

339
00:20:00,343 --> 00:20:04,030
Tanaka-san, thank you for everything.

340
00:20:04,054 --> 00:20:06,903
What’s gotten into you all of a sudden?

341
00:20:06,926 --> 00:20:09,860
Oh, I just wanted to say it.

342
00:20:09,883 --> 00:20:12,376
Well then, let’s head to the office.

343
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:15,041
Yes, let’s go.

344
00:20:15,064 --> 00:20:19,135
I am Rin.

345
00:20:19,159 --> 00:20:22,526
This is Tokyo.

346
00:20:22,549 --> 00:20:27,116
The language barrier still exists.

347
00:20:27,139 --> 00:20:32,005
But no wall is too high to overcome.

348
00:20:32,028 --> 00:20:37,062
I will express myself in my own words.

349
00:20:37,085 --> 00:20:42,334
I will live by my own designs.

350
00:20:42,358 --> 00:20:47,295
My story begins here.

351
00:20:47,318 --> 00:20:52,756
Today, a new day begins.

352
00:21:02,416 --> 00:21:03,916
Scene 1: The Start of a New Day

353
00:21:03,916 --> 00:21:07,312
Listening Test

354
00:21:07,312 --> 00:21:11,289
I open my eyes.

355
00:21:11,289 --> 00:21:16,789
V + Vます = do...
目 (め) = eye
開(あ)ける (open) ↔ 閉(し)める (close)

356
00:21:16,812 --> 00:21:20,712
Listening Test

357
00:21:20,712 --> 00:21:25,305
All I see is a white ceiling.

358
00:21:25,305 --> 00:21:31,605
Nが + 見(み)えます = can see N
天井 (てんじょう) = ceiling

359
00:21:31,628 --> 00:21:35,761
Listening Test

360
00:21:35,761 --> 00:21:40,661
This is Tokyo.

361
00:21:40,661 --> 00:21:47,361
N1は + N2です = N1 is N2
ここ = here

362
00:21:47,384 --> 00:21:51,818
Listening Test

363
00:21:51,818 --> 00:21:57,084
My name is Rin.

364
00:21:57,084 --> 00:22:04,265
N1の + N2 = N1's N2
名前 (なまえ) = name

365
00:22:04,289 --> 00:22:07,522
Listening Test

366
00:22:07,522 --> 00:22:11,258
I came here from America.

367
00:22:11,258 --> 00:22:16,424
Nから + 来(き)ました = came from N
来(く)る = to come

368
00:22:16,447 --> 00:22:19,955
Listening Test

369
00:22:19,955 --> 00:22:24,073
The room is so quiet.

370
00:22:24,073 --> 00:22:29,740
なAです = is/are... (e.g., 'quiet' or 'lively') 
部屋 (へや) = room 
静か (quiet) ↔ 賑やか (lively)

371
00:22:29,763 --> 00:22:34,149
Listening Test

372
00:22:34,149 --> 00:22:39,382
All I can hear is the ticking of the clock.

373
00:22:39,382 --> 00:22:46,496
Nだけ + が + 聞こえます = can only hear N 
時計 (とけい) = clock 
音 (おと) = sound

374
00:22:46,519 --> 00:22:49,669
Listening Test

375
00:22:49,669 --> 00:22:53,345
I open the window.

376
00:22:53,345 --> 00:22:58,414
Nを + Vます = do N (e.g., 'open the window') 
窓 (まど) = window

377
00:22:58,438 --> 00:23:02,908
Listening Test

378
00:23:02,908 --> 00:23:08,241
A cold breeze blows in.

379
00:23:08,241 --> 00:23:15,511
いA + N = adjective + N (e.g., 'cold wind') 
冷たい (cold) ↔ 温かい (warm) 
風 (かぜ) = wind

380
00:23:15,534 --> 00:23:19,801
Listening Test

381
00:23:19,801 --> 00:23:24,868
A new day begins.

382
00:23:24,868 --> 00:23:31,771
Nが + Vます = N starts (e.g., 'the new day begins') 
新しい (new) ↔ 古い (old) 
始まる = to begin

383
00:23:31,794 --> 00:23:36,827
Listening Test

384
00:23:36,827 --> 00:23:42,860
Today, I’ll keep living in this big city.

385
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:51,027
Vて + いきます = continue to do... (e.g., 'the city keeps growing') 
大きい (big) ↔ 小さい (small) 
街 (まち) = city

386
00:23:51,050 --> 00:23:54,483
Listening Test

387
00:23:54,483 --> 00:23:58,517
I sip my coffee.

388
00:23:58,517 --> 00:24:04,024
Nを + 飲みます = drink N 
飲む = to drink

389
00:24:04,048 --> 00:24:07,404
Listening Test

390
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:11,339
It’s warm.

391
00:24:11,339 --> 00:24:16,772
いAです = it is... (e.g., 'it's warm') 
温かい (warm) ↔ 冷たい (cold)

392
00:24:16,795 --> 00:24:21,341
Listening Test

393
00:24:21,341 --> 00:24:26,774
I get ready and head outside.

394
00:24:26,774 --> 00:24:34,167
Vて + Vます = do... and... (e.g., 'prepare and go outside') 
準備 (じゅんび) = preparation 
外 (outside) ↔ 中 (inside)

395
00:24:34,191 --> 00:24:37,491
Listening Test

396
00:24:37,491 --> 00:24:41,357
I walk to the station.

397
00:24:41,357 --> 00:24:46,659
Nまで = to N (e.g., 'walk to the station') 
駅 (えき) = station 
歩く = to walk

398
00:24:46,683 --> 00:24:50,383
Listening Test

399
00:24:50,383 --> 00:24:54,737
There are so many people.

400
00:24:54,737 --> 00:25:00,712
Nがたくさん + います = there are many N 
たくさん = many, a lot

401
00:25:00,735 --> 00:25:04,835
Listening Test

402
00:25:04,835 --> 00:25:09,702
Where is everyone going?

403
00:25:09,702 --> 00:25:16,369
Nへ + 行きますか = go to N? (e.g., 'are you going to the park?') 
行く (go) ↔ 来る (come)

404
00:25:16,392 --> 00:25:20,058
Listening Test

405
00:25:20,058 --> 00:25:24,369
No one knows me.

406
00:25:24,369 --> 00:25:30,277
誰も + Vません = nobody... (e.g., 'nobody knows') 
誰も = nobody 
知る = to know

407
00:25:30,301 --> 00:25:33,697
Listening Test

408
00:25:33,697 --> 00:25:37,683
It feels a little lonely.

409
00:25:37,683 --> 00:25:43,183
少し + いAです = a little... (e.g., 'a little lonely') 
少し = a little 
寂しい = lonely

410
00:25:43,206 --> 00:25:47,874
Listening Test

411
00:25:47,874 --> 00:25:53,440
Oh, good morning, Rin!

412
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:05,937
Listening Test

413
00:26:05,937 --> 00:26:11,770
Oh, good morning, Mr. Tanaka!

414
00:26:19,743 --> 00:26:22,610
Listening Test

415
00:26:22,610 --> 00:26:25,921
You’re early again today.

416
00:26:25,921 --> 00:26:30,500
いAですね = ..., isn't it? (e.g., 'it's early, isn't it?') 
早い (early) ↔ 遅い (late)

417
00:26:30,523 --> 00:26:35,190
Listening Test

418
00:26:35,190 --> 00:26:40,747
Yeah, I love the morning air.

419
00:26:40,747 --> 00:26:48,327
Nが + 好きですから = because I like N (e.g., 'because I like the morning air') 
朝 (morning) ↔ 夜 (night) 
空気 (くうき) = air

420
00:26:48,350 --> 00:26:51,784
Listening Test

421
00:26:51,784 --> 00:26:55,777
I see. That’s nice.

422
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:05,600
Listening Test

423
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:10,709
You’re always early too, Mr. Tanaka.

424
00:27:10,709 --> 00:27:17,680
Nも + いAですね = N is also... (e.g., 'it's always quiet too') 
いつも = always

425
00:27:17,703 --> 00:27:23,137
Listening Test

426
00:27:23,137 --> 00:27:29,656
Yeah, I prefer the morning trains.

427
00:27:29,656 --> 00:27:38,530
Nが + 好きです = I like N 
電車 (でんしゃ) = train 
好き (like) ↔ 嫌い (dislike)

428
00:27:38,553 --> 00:27:41,495
Listening Test

429
00:27:41,495 --> 00:27:44,929
There are fewer people.

430
00:27:44,929 --> 00:27:49,642
いAですから = because... (e.g., 'because it's crowded') 
多い (many) ↔ 少ない (few)

431
00:27:49,665 --> 00:27:55,365
Listening Test

432
00:27:55,365 --> 00:28:02,198
True. Crowded trains can be a little scary.

433
00:28:02,198 --> 00:28:11,498
Nは + いAです = N is... (e.g., 'the crowded train is scary') 
満員電車 (まんいんでんしゃ) = crowded train 
怖い = scary

434
00:28:11,521 --> 00:28:16,317
Listening Test

435
00:28:16,317 --> 00:28:22,050
Even Japanese people don’t like packed trains.

436
00:28:22,050 --> 00:28:29,837
Nは + 好きじゃありません = don't like N 
日本人 (にほんじん) = Japanese person

437
00:28:29,861 --> 00:28:33,577
Listening Test

438
00:28:33,577 --> 00:28:37,955
Really? That makes me feel better.

439
00:28:37,955 --> 00:28:43,953
Vました = did... (e.g., 'felt relieved') 
安心する = to feel relieved

440
00:28:43,976 --> 00:28:46,914
Listening Test

441
00:28:46,914 --> 00:28:50,348
Here comes the train.

442
00:28:50,348 --> 00:28:55,081
Vましたよ = ...arrived! (e.g., 'I've arrived!') 
来る = to come

443
00:28:55,104 --> 00:28:58,494
Listening Test

444
00:28:58,494 --> 00:29:02,463
Yeah, let’s go together.

445
00:29:02,463 --> 00:29:07,930
一緒に + Vましょう = let's do... together (e.g., 'let's go together') 
一緒に = together

446
00:29:07,953 --> 00:29:11,553
Listening Test

447
00:29:11,553 --> 00:29:15,819
I heard Mr. Tanaka’s voice.

448
00:29:15,819 --> 00:29:21,653
Nを + 聞きました = heard N (e.g., 'heard a voice') 
声 (こえ) = voice 
聞く = to hear

449
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:26,212
Listening Test

450
00:29:26,212 --> 00:29:31,645
The loneliness faded a little.

451
00:29:31,645 --> 00:29:39,019
Nが + Vました = N faded/disappeared (e.g., 'the feeling disappeared') 
気持ち = feeling 
消える = to disappear

452
00:29:39,042 --> 00:29:42,520
Listening Test

453
00:29:42,520 --> 00:29:46,596
I’m not alone.

454
00:29:46,596 --> 00:29:52,230
Nじゃありません = am not N (e.g., 'I'm not alone') 
一人 (ひとり) = alone

455
00:29:52,253 --> 00:29:55,953
Listening Test

456
00:29:55,953 --> 00:30:00,286
Off to work I go.

457
00:30:00,286 --> 00:30:06,219
Nへ + 行きます = go to N (e.g., 'go to work') 
仕事 (しごと) = work

458
00:30:06,242 --> 00:30:07,742
Scene 2: The Kanji Barrier and Work

459
00:30:07,742 --> 00:30:10,682
Listening Test

460
00:30:10,682 --> 00:30:14,116
I’ve arrived at the office.

461
00:30:14,116 --> 00:30:18,816
N に 着きます = arrive at N (e.g., 'arrive at the company') 
会社 (かいしゃ) = company

462
00:30:18,839 --> 00:30:21,595
Listening Test

463
00:30:21,595 --> 00:30:24,772
I open my laptop.

464
00:30:24,772 --> 00:30:29,205
N を 開きます = open N (e.g., 'open the door') 
開く (open) ↔ 閉じる (close)

465
00:30:29,228 --> 00:30:32,561
Listening Test

466
00:30:32,561 --> 00:30:36,461
There are so many emails.

467
00:30:36,461 --> 00:30:41,819
N が あります = there is/are N (e.g., 'there are many') 
たくさん = many / a lot

468
00:30:41,843 --> 00:30:45,237
Listening Test

469
00:30:45,237 --> 00:30:49,206
All in Japanese.

470
00:30:49,206 --> 00:30:54,673
N です = it is N (e.g., 'it's all done') 
全部 (ぜんぶ) = all

471
00:30:54,696 --> 00:30:58,662
Listening Test

472
00:30:58,662 --> 00:31:03,362
Kanji is really tough.

473
00:31:03,362 --> 00:31:09,796
いA です = be いA (e.g., 'it's difficult') 
難しい (difficult) ↔ 易しい (easy)

474
00:31:09,819 --> 00:31:14,052
Listening Test

475
00:31:14,052 --> 00:31:19,085
I work in design.

476
00:31:19,085 --> 00:31:25,952
Vています = be doing V (e.g., 'I'm working') 
仕事 (しごと) = work / job

477
00:31:25,975 --> 00:31:29,042
Listening Test

478
00:31:29,042 --> 00:31:32,584
Design is what I’m good at.

479
00:31:32,584 --> 00:31:37,484
N は 得意です = be good at N (e.g., 'I'm good at languages') 
得意 (good at) ↔ 苦手 (poor at)

480
00:31:37,506 --> 00:31:41,573
Listening Test

481
00:31:41,573 --> 00:31:46,367
But the language barrier is high.

482
00:31:46,367 --> 00:31:52,916
N1 の N2 = N2 of N1 (e.g., 'the meaning of the word') 
言葉 (ことば) = word / language 
高い (high) ↔ 低い (low)

483
00:31:52,940 --> 00:31:56,806
Listening Test

484
00:31:56,806 --> 00:32:01,347
Sometimes, I feel like crying.

485
00:32:01,347 --> 00:32:07,581
Vたくなります = feel like doing V (e.g., 'sometimes I feel like crying') 
時々 (ときどき) = sometimes 
泣く = to cry

486
00:32:07,604 --> 00:32:11,070
Listening Test

487
00:32:11,070 --> 00:32:15,137
I let out a big sigh.

488
00:32:15,137 --> 00:32:20,719
N が 出ます = N comes out (e.g., 'a big sigh comes out') 
大きい (big) ↔ 小さい (small) 
ため息 (いき) = sigh

489
00:32:20,743 --> 00:32:24,243
Listening Test

490
00:32:24,243 --> 00:32:28,348
Rin, are you okay?

491
00:32:28,348 --> 00:32:33,981
なA ですか = Are you なA? (e.g., 'are you alright?') 
大丈夫 = alright / okay

492
00:32:34,004 --> 00:32:39,271
Listening Test

493
00:32:39,271 --> 00:32:45,586
Oh, Tanaka-san. Yes, it's alright.

494
00:32:54,242 --> 00:32:58,342
Listening Test

495
00:32:58,342 --> 00:33:03,179
You were sighing deeply.

496
00:33:03,179 --> 00:33:09,812
Vていました = was doing V (e.g., 'was sighing') 
ため息をつく = breathe a sigh

497
00:33:09,835 --> 00:33:15,069
Listening Test

498
00:33:15,069 --> 00:33:21,306
I'm sorry. Some kanji are a bit difficult for me.

499
00:33:21,306 --> 00:33:29,818
いA です = be いA (e.g., 'it's a little cold') 
少し = a little

500
00:33:29,841 --> 00:33:32,508
Listening Test

501
00:33:32,508 --> 00:33:35,574
Which kanji?

502
00:33:35,574 --> 00:33:39,808
どの N ですか = Which N is it? (e.g., 'which one is it?')

503
00:33:39,831 --> 00:33:43,189
Listening Test

504
00:33:43,189 --> 00:33:47,122
The kanji in this email.

505
00:33:47,122 --> 00:33:52,555
この N = this N (e.g., 'this book')

506
00:33:52,578 --> 00:33:58,012
Listening Test

507
00:33:58,012 --> 00:34:04,512
Ah, this one reads 'kakunin'.

508
00:34:04,512 --> 00:34:13,345
N と 読みます = read as N (e.g., 'read as confirmation') 
確認 (かくにん) = confirmation / check

509
00:34:13,368 --> 00:34:16,201
Listening Test

510
00:34:16,201 --> 00:34:19,471
'Kakunin'?

511
00:34:19,471 --> 00:34:24,005
N ですか = Is it N? (e.g., 'is it correct?')

512
